meta {
  name: S11b workflow definitions
  seq: 11
}

docs {
  Story S11b, TICK-337, P3-41 (TICK-710). A tenant admin publishes a workflow definition version and reads it back; the server assigns the step ids and keeps them across versions. Needs `tools/seed.sh`. Story users: `admin@tenant-a` is tenant A's admin, `agent@tenant-a` is Alice, `agent@tenant-b` is Bob. Tenant B's admin getting the 404 for tenant A's key is asserted in CI (`TestWorkflowDefinitions*`), not here: the seed has no tenant B admin. Runs again on the same stack: every pass uses a new definition key. S11b.17 to S11b.30 (P3-44, TICK-713) are the story criteria: the demo definition `s11b_demo` (on `record.created` of an incident, wait 1 minute, set `state=in_progress`) runs on the stack's nava-worker, so they take about 70 s; S11b.30 retires it again. The stack case `s11b_workflows` runs this folder on a fresh stack and checks the database behind each criterion.
}
